    longDef: "Deep learning uses artificial neural networks with many successive layers. Each layer progressively extracts more abstract representations of the input data — for example, edges then shapes then objects in an image. The very rich representational capacity, combined with massive data volumes and modern computing power (GPU/TPU), enables performance that was unattainable fifteen years ago.\n\nDeep learning underpins most of the most visible modern AI systems: image recognition, machine translation, voice assistants, generative models like GPT-4 or Claude. Its power comes with high training costs, substantial data needs, and greater interpretation difficulty compared to simpler models.",
