    longDef: "An Autonomous Mobile Robot (AMR) is capable of dynamically planning its trajectories, avoiding obstacles, and adapting to a changing environment — humans circulating, pallets moved, evolving warehouse configuration. This adaptation capacity distinguishes AMRs from classical AGVs (Automated Guided Vehicles) which follow materialized paths (rails, ground lines, magnetic markers).\n\nAMRs have become the backbone of modern warehouse logistics. Amazon Robotics operates several generations of AMRs (Hercules, Pegasus, Sequoia) that transport entire shelves in distribution centers. Beyond the warehouse, AMRs are deploying in healthcare (medication transport in hospitals), industry (inter-station handling), and service (last-meter delivery).",
